{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויסב אלהים את העם דרך המדבר", :translit "va-yasav elohim et ha-am derekh ha-midbar", :gloss "And Elohim led the people by the way of the wilderness"} {:he "שערך להם שלחן", :translit "she-erakh la-hem shulhan", :gloss "that He set a table for them"} {:he "והסיבן לאכול", :translit "ve-hisivan le-ekhol", :gloss "and seated them reclining to eat"} {:he "כד\"א", :translit "ka-da-amar", :gloss "as that which is said"} {:he "היוכל אל לערוך שלחן במדבר", :translit "ha-yukhal el le-arokh shulhan ba-midbar", :gloss "Can El prepare a table in the wilderness"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking ויסב (led/seated) to הסיבן (reclining at meal) via Psalm 78:19's שלחן במדבר"}], :frame {:text "The phrase ויסב ordinarily means 'He turned/led the people.' Ba'al HaTurim reads it as connected to הסבה, the act of reclining at a banquet. He links this to Psalm 78:19, where Israel asks 'Can El prepare a table in the wilderness?' (Psalm 78:19). The verse in Psalms is traditionally understood as Israel's complaint in the desert regarding food (Psalm 78:19).", :sources ["Psalm 78:19"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וחמושים", :translit "ve-chamushim", :gloss "and chamushim"} {:he "מזויינים", :translit "mezuyanim", :gloss "armed"} {:he "על שם חמשה כלי זיין", :translit "al shem chamishah keli zayin", :gloss "on account of five weapons"} {:he "הנזכרים בפסוק", :translit "ha-nizkarim ba-pasuk", :gloss "mentioned in the verse"} {:he "מגן וצנה ורומח וחצים ומקל יד", :translit "magen ve-tzinah ve-romach ve-chatzim ve-makel yad", :gloss "shield and buckler and spear and arrows and hand-staff"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Derives chamushim from chamishah (five), referring to five weapons listed in a verse"}], :frame {:text "The word chamushim is explained by Targum Onkelos as 'armed' (Targum Onkelos on Exodus 13:18). The five weapons Ba'al HaTurim enumerates — מגן, צנה, רומח, חצים, מקל יד — correspond to items of military equipment mentioned in biblical passages such as Psalms 35:2 and other verses.", :sources ["Targum Onkelos Exodus 13:18" "Psalms 35:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking ויסב (led/seated) to הסיבן (reclining at meal) via Psalm 78:19's שלחן במדבר", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Derives chamushim from chamishah (five), referring to five weapons listed in a verse", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:41.606131426Z", :model "glm-5.2"}